    "done_when": "reckon/mcp.py no longer emits the multiple-active-sprints finding, and no other reader treats two active sprints as an error. A test pushes two sprints on a synthetic distributed project under a temporary config home, asserts both keep active, and asserts the audit on that project reports no multiple-active-sprints finding. active_sprint_id follows the live sprint when crews exist and falls back to the stored status when none do, with tests/test_active_sprint_follows_live_crew.py passing. skills/reckon-sprint/SKILL.md no longer says pushing demotes the previous sprint or that a second active sprint is an error, and states the new contract in one paragraph. Every existing test that asserted the finding or demotion is updated to the new contract in the same commit, and the manifest names each. The declared mutation, restoring the finding, fails the new audit case with its log recorded. The sprint, roadmap, audit and mcp test files touched or named show zero added failures by id against the dispatch base, run with the absolute venv python and a neutral basetemp on node-local /tmp. baseline_suite and after_suite are one-line JSON with revision, tree, full command, exit_status, absolute log_path, completed, failure_count and failure_ids, negative_control_log is a top-level absolute path, and a tests: field is recorded",
